claims:
8. A method for performing a search to identify web sites that relate to a search term based on content within the web sites, the method being performed by a web host having members and comprising:
determining whether a web page of a web site is accessed by a member of a web host; 
conditioning automatic collection of content appearing on the web page based upon whether the web page has been accessed by a member of a web host; 
storing the content that was automatically collected for comparison against search terms received; 
receiving at least one search term; 
comparing the search term with the content stored from within at least two different web pages from different web sites to determine whether matches exist; and 
displaying results based on the matches that are determined to exist, the results including at least one web site identifier.

23. A method for performing a search to identify web sites that relate to a search term based on text within the web sites, the method comprising:
receiving at least one search term; 
comparing the search term with electronic information within at least one electronic information store to determine whether matches exist, where the electronic information within the at least one electronic information store includes text displayed by different web pages from different web sites and titles, descriptions, and addresses of the different web sites such that comparing the search term comprises comparing the search term with at least one of the text, the titles, the descriptions, and the addresses of the web sites; 
displaying results based on the matches that are determined to exist, the results including identifiers for several web sites; and 
ranking identifiers for the several web sites based on whether the matches occur with at least one of the text, the titles, the descriptions, and the addresses of the web sites.
